OL,3,AFounder of collapsed Chinese property
OL,4,Agiant Evergrande sentenced to life in
OL,5,Aprison
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe founder of Evergrande, the property
OL,8,Fgiant at the centre of China's housing
OL,9,Fmarket slump, has been sentenced to
OL,10,Flife in prison and had all of his
OL,11,Fpersonal property confiscated.
OL,13,FHui Ka Yan pleaded guilty in April to
OL,14,Fseveral charges, including embezzlement
OL,15,Fof assets and corporate bribery.
OL,17,FShenzhen Intermediate People's Court
OL,18,Falso fined his former companies a total
OL,19,Fof 15.82bn yuan (#1.73bn; $2.35bn) over
OL,20,Fmultiple crimes, including falsifying
OL,21,Frecords and concealing debt.
OL,23,APub: 20-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
